), and it has a major European port. Due to its long and culturally rich history, the city of Antwerp houses interesting historical buildings from different historical periods and numerous museums. Antwerp is also known as the global diamond trade hub: more than 70% of all diamonds are traded in Antwerp. Antwerp has grown to become a trendy city, attracting Flemish and foreign artists, writers, intellectuals, and actors.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Antwerp","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Antwerp","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Antwerp is the capital of the eponymous province in the region of Flanders in Belgium. Plantin-Moretus House-Workshops-Museum Complex, Koninklijk Museum voor Schone Kunsten and Rubenshuis lead its 12 sights. Plan two days, ideally in May to September.","short_src":"composed","facts":{"population":529247,"visit_h":16.8}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-plantin-moretus-house-workshops-museum-complex","name":"Plantin-Moretus House-Workshops-Museum Complex","kind":"Museum","lat":51.2185,"lon":4.39816,"dist_km":0.3,"sig":2.969,"rank_score":11.96,"resolved_by":"catalogue","fact":"Printing museum in Antwerp, Belgium","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Library_of_Plantin-Moretus_Museum_in_Antwerp.jpg/960px-Library_of_Plantin-Moretus_Museum_in_Antwerp.jpg","author":"The original uploader was Meltwaterfalls at English Wikipedia","licence":"Public domain","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Library_of_Plantin-Moretus_Museum_in_Antwerp.jpg","w":2032,"h":1354,"ok_print":true},"wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plantin%E2%80%93Moretus_Museum","heritage":true,"merged_from":["Museum Plantin-Moretus"]},{"id":"hl-koninklijk-museum-voor-schone-kunsten","name":"Koninklijk Museum voor Schone Kunsten","kind":"Museum","lat":51.20847,"lon":4.39488,"dist_km":1.3,"sig":2.962,"rank_score":11.36,"resolved_by":"catalogue","fact":"kunstmuseum in Antwerpen, België","image":{"url":"https://uploa